PART P -- the PRIMARY route: everything collapses onto phi_K itself.
  (P1-P6 are the proof as ATTEMPT.md §3-§4 states it; S1-S11 below are
   the equivalent central-binomial route, kept as a cross-check.)

  [OK  ] P0  phi_K == 4^K / ((2K+1) C(2K,K)),  K symbolic
  [OK  ] P1  (K+2)4^K/(4(2K+1)C(2K,K)) - 1/2  ==  [(K+2)phi_K - 2]/4,  K symbolic
  [OK  ] P2  [(K-1)!K!/(2K)!](4^K - C(2K,K))/2  ==  [(2K+1)phi_K - 1]/(2K),  K symbolic
  [OK  ] P3  phi_{K+1}/phi_K == (2K+2)/(2K+3),  K symbolic
  [OK  ] P4  v_{K+1}/v_K - 1 == K/((K+2)(2K+3))  > 0 for K>=1,  K symbolic
  [OK  ] P5  v_1 == 2 exactly (the equality case; c_1 = 0)
  [OK  ] P6a phi_K == int_0^1 (1-x^2)^K dx  (checked K=0..12 by symbolic integration)  :: mismatches: []
  [OK  ] P6b phi_K == prod_{j=1}^K 2j/(2j+1) follows from P3 with phi_0 = 1
  [OK  ] P7a v_{j+1} - v_j == j*phi_j/(2j+3),  j symbolic  (the telescoping increment)
  [OK  ] P7b c_K == (1/4) sum_{j=1}^{K-1} j*phi_j/(2j+3), exact, K=1..400  :: mismatches: []
  [OK  ] P7c every term j*phi_j/(2j+3) is strictly positive (phi_j > 0, j >= 1)

PART S -- the equivalent central-binomial route (cross-check)

  [OK  ] S1  prod_{i=1}^{k+1}(K+i) == (K+k+1)!/K!,  K,k symbolic
  [OK  ] S2  summand == (K-1)!K!/((K-1-k)!(K+k+1)!),  K,k symbolic
  [OK  ] S3  (2K)!/((K-1-k)!(K+k+1)!) == C(2K,K+k+1),  K,k symbolic
  [OK  ] S4a C(2K,j) == C(2K,2K-j),  K,j symbolic
  [OK  ] S4b sum_{j=0}^{2K} C(2K,j) == 4^K  (binomial theorem)
  [OK  ] S4c assembled: 2*sum_{j=K+1}^{2K}C(2K,j) == 4^K - C(2K,K), K=1..300
  [OK  ] S5  (3/4)phi_K*(2K)!/((K-1)!K!) == (3/4)4^K K/(2K+1),  K symbolic
  [OK  ] S6  c_K == (K+2)4^K/(4(2K+1)C(2K,K)) - 1/2,  K symbolic
  [OK  ] S7  u_{K+1}/u_K == 2(K+1)(K+3)/((K+2)(2K+3)),  K symbolic  :: sympy got 2*(K + 1)*(K + 3)/((K + 2)*(2*K + 3))
  [OK  ] S8  2(K+1)(K+3) - (K+2)(2K+3) == K   (>0 for K>=1),  K symbolic
  [OK  ] S9  u_1 == 1  (equivalently c_1 == 0)
  [OK  ] S9' c_K at K=1 is 0

